KONOHAGAKURE — GENIN TEAM ASSIGNMENT POLICY

Upon graduation, genin are organized into three-member cells, each led by a jonin-sensei — the standard four-person squad.

Policy:
- Cells are composed to balance abilities: typically a strong offensive nin, a support/control nin, and a versatile member, so the team is capable across roles.
- Team scores from the Academy inform balancing; the top-scoring graduate may be paired with the lowest to even the cells (as with Team 7).
- The jonin-sensei administers a final test of the sensei's own design (e.g., the bell test) to confirm the cell is fit for duty; teamwork over individual skill is the deciding measure.
- Traditional clan trios (Ino-Shika-Cho) may be preserved across generations.

Cell composition is set by the Academy and the Jonin Commander's office and confirmed by the Hokage.
Issued by the Administration Building.
